// Multiple Failed Logons (burst) — Windows Security Event 4625
// Fires when a single account accumulates >= 10 failed logons
// inside any 5-minute window.
//
// Runs unchanged against:
//   - Microsoft Sentinel / Log Analytics  (real SecurityEvent table)
//   - Azure Data Explorer free cluster     (mirror table, see test-data/adx-setup.kql)
// because the ADX test table is created with the same name and columns.
//
// Gotchas exercised here (see ../../references/SPL-to-KQL-reference.md):
//   - aggregates are named explicitly (failures, hosts, src_ips) — never rely on count_
//   - filter (where EventID) sits ABOVE summarize
//   - bin() on TimeGenerated replaces SPL's | bin _time span=5m

SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4625
| summarize failures = count(), hosts = dcount(Computer), src_ips = dcount(IpAddress)
    by Account, bin(TimeGenerated, 5m)
| where failures >= 10
| order by failures desc
